{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21f37e39d99b57bc5b33", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Chemical Bonding and Molecular Structure - Test 1", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 37, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d92535c9"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253583", "title": "Chemistry Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925351a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e567ac499d1e49588f95f5"], "concepts": ["61ab78816fe44bfe0fe4a16f"], "question": {"text": "Identify the species having one <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></math> -bond and maximum number of canonical forms from the following :"}, "options": [{"id": "df72d2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925351b"}, {"id": "f0ad33", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925351c"}, {"id": "45370c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925351d"}, {"id": "4e479e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>CO</mi><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925351e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925351f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["6117b90867dbe2603c3e9080"], "concepts": ["6117b90767dbe2603c3e8fa9"], "question": {"text": "Which of the following is least ionic?"}, "options": [{"id": "4befac", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BaCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253520"}, {"id": "752d60", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AgCl</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253521"}, {"id": "dabef8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KCl</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253522"}, {"id": "d4aaff", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CoCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253523"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253524", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b76"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e58"], "question": {"text": "In 3, 3-dimethylhex-1-ene-4-yne, there are _______ $\\mathrm{sp}^3$, _______ $\\mathrm{sp}^2$ and _______ sp hybridised carbon atoms respectively :"}, "options": [{"id": "de3dc5", "text": "4,2,2", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253525"}, {"id": "c44cd7", "text": "3,3,2", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253526"}, {"id": "158e4c", "text": "2,4,2", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253527"}, {"id": "6b4cda", "text": "2,2,4", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253528"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253529", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e8"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b64"], "question": {"text": "According to molecular orbital theory, which of the following is true with respect to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>Li</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>Li</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math> ?"}, "options": [{"id": "812ff2", "text": "<math><mi>L</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mi> </mi></math> is stable and <math><mi>L</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mi> </mi></math> is unstable", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925352a"}, {"id": "a36504", "text": "Both are unstable", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925352b"}, {"id": "8f2768", "text": "Both are stable", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925352c"}, {"id": "fe8b23", "text": "<math><mi>L</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mi> </mi></math> is unstable and <math><mi>L</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mi> </mi></math> is stable", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925352d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925352e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f44"], "concepts": ["6162fb836ed13040ec84fc98"], "question": {"text": "<p>Arrange the following in increasing order of their covalent character.</p><p>(A)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CaF</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>(B) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CaCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>(C)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CaBr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>(D)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CaI</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "b1610f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925352f"}, {"id": "8c2727", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253530"}, {"id": "0fc636", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253531"}, {"id": "79df3b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253532"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253533", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4771"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4727"], "question": {"text": "<p><strong>Statement I:-</strong> Dipole moment is a vector quantity and by convention it is depicted by a small arrow with tail on the negative centre and head pointing towards the positive centre.</p><p><strong>Statement II:-</strong> The crossed arrow of the dipole moment symbolizes the direction of the shift of charges in the molecules.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:-</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "2c0634", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are correct.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253534"}, {"id": "46e639", "text": "Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253535"}, {"id": "5f9c5e", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253536"}, {"id": "411a93", "text": "Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253537"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253538", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fbdd66f9ce3f243b567c"], "concepts": ["61ab79db6fe44bfe0fe4b3bb"], "question": {"text": "If the boiling point of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>373</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>,&nbsp;and&nbsp; the boiling point of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> will be :"}, "options": [{"id": "814a5b", "text": "less than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253539"}, {"id": "5f10fa", "text": "equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>373</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925353a"}, {"id": "b24c00", "text": "more than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>373</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925353b"}, {"id": "391f14", "text": "greater than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> but less than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>373</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925353c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925353d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e5676a499d1e49588f8f0c"], "concepts": ["617aa9e9ef3fe65ad8e837de"], "question": {"text": "The correct option with order of melting points of the pairs \\((\\mathrm{Mn}, \\mathrm{Fe}),(\\mathrm{Tc}, \\mathrm{Ru})\\) and \\((\\mathrm{Re}, \\mathrm{Os})\\) is :"}, "options": [{"id": "3579a9", "text": "\\(\\mathrm{Fe} \\lt \\mathrm{Mn}, \\mathrm{Ru} \\lt \\mathrm{Tc}\\) and \\(\\mathrm{Re} \\lt \\mathrm{Os}\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925353e"}, {"id": "375b6b", "text": "\\(\\mathrm{Mn} \\lt \\mathrm{Fe}, \\mathrm{Tc} \\lt \\mathrm{Ru}\\) and \\(\\mathrm{Os} \\lt \\mathrm{Re}\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925353f"}, {"id": "fa8705", "text": "\\(\\mathrm{Mn} \\lt \\mathrm{Fe}, \\mathrm{Tc} \\lt \\mathrm{Ru}\\) and \\(\\mathrm{Re} \\lt \\mathrm{Os}\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253540"}, {"id": "fbcd0e", "text": "\\(\\mathrm{Fe} \\lt \\mathrm{Mn}, \\mathrm{Ru} \\lt \\mathrm{Tc}\\) and \\(\\mathrm{Os} \\lt \\mathrm{Re}\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253541"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253542", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60d3035eaf049203d8536690"], "concepts": ["6162fb836ed13040ec84fc9a"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements:\nStatement I: \\(\\mathrm{N}\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_3\\right)_3\\) and \\(\\mathrm{P}\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_3\\right)_3\\) can act as ligands to form transition metal complexes.\nStatement II: As N and P are from same group, the nature of bonding of \\(\\mathrm{N}\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_3\\right)_3\\) and \\(\\mathrm{P}\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_3\\right)_3\\) is always same with transition metals.\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:"}, "options": [{"id": "7aca04", "text": "Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253543"}, {"id": "455fe5", "text": "Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253544"}, {"id": "dc8b76", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are correct.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253545"}, {"id": "e09cb9", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253546"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253547", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e567ac499d1e49588f95f5"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95d8"], "question": {"text": "Which of the following pair of molecules contain odd electron molecule and an expanded octet molecule?"}, "options": [{"id": "272f87", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SF</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253548"}, {"id": "718bf8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NO</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253549"}, {"id": "7e2782", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SF</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925354a"}, {"id": "58106b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NO</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925354b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925354c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b76"], "concepts": ["6117b88f67dbe2603c3e80be"], "question": {"text": "The hybridisations of the atomic orbitals of nitrogen in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup></math> respectively are."}, "options": [{"id": "7d00dd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sp</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925354d"}, {"id": "15fb87", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sp</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925354e"}, {"id": "e6caa7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sp</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925354f"}, {"id": "efa3af", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sp</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253550"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253551", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fbdd66f9ce3f243b567c"], "concepts": ["617aa9e9ef3fe65ad8e837f2"], "question": {"text": "Decreasing order of the hydrogen bonding in following forms of water is correctly represented by<br />A. Liquid water<br />B. Ice<br />C. Impure water"}, "options": [{"id": "df8eaf", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253552"}, {"id": "b85dcf", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253553"}, {"id": "62f440", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253554"}, {"id": "124127", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253555"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253556", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e8"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52be"], "question": {"text": "If the magnetic moment of a di-oxygen species is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1.73&#160;</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>.</mo></math>, it may be"}, "options": [{"id": "e87065", "text": "<math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math> or <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253557"}, {"id": "51037c", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> or <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253558"}, {"id": "07fa9b", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> or <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253559"}, {"id": "195ccd", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math> or <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925355a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925355b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a