athML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> are correct and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is the correct explanation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253567"}, {"id": "c68d3b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is not correct but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253568"}, {"id": "b0f0d2", "text": "Both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> are correct but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NOT</mi></math> the correct explanation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d9253569"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f382ee0e063d925356a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60d3035eaf049203d8536690"], "concepts": ["6162fb836ed13040ec84fc9a"], "question": {"text": "The correct statement among the following is:"}, "options": [{"id": "404fee", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> is planar and less basic than <math><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</m